Back End Java Developer
We are seeking a seasoned Senior Backend Engineer who is passionate about designing and delivering robust solutions. This role involves close collaboration within a dynamic team and a strong focus on building scalable backend microservices for data platforms that empower our clients to access and leverage data with ease. 
The Expertise and Skills You Bring
•	6+ years of experience developing enterprise solutions across multiple technology platforms, programming languages, and Data platform.
•	Expertise in backend development building in Java / Python with API first approach for scalable environment.
•	Deep understanding of APIs, UI development, infrastructure, security, and emerging technologies.
•	Expert knowledge of Agile development methodologies and DevOps practices.
•	Strong experience using Java, Java EE/Jakarta EE, Spring Framework/Spring Boot, Kafka, and modern web application technologies.
•	Solid understanding of relational databases (PostgreSQL, SQL/Oracle)
•	Experience in data pipelines ETL/ELT tools, control-M
•	Hands-on experience with cloud platforms such as AWS or Azure, including deployment and architecture best practices.
•	Proven experience designing and working with microservices architectures.
•	Ability to work independently and collaboratively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.
•	Strong critical thinking skills with the ability to translate business needs into scalable technology solutions.
•	Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science or a related field.
The Team
Fidelity Institutional Technology (FIT) is the engine behind Fidelity’s Institutional business units, delivering the infrastructure and products that empower our partners to thrive in their markets. Within FIT, the Managed & Advisory Solutions team—part of the broader FI Wealth Management Domain—focuses on developing and supporting products that enable managed product distribution both on and off platform.
As a key member of this fast-paced team, you will contribute to the development of robust applications that support the evolving needs of our Managed & Advisory Solutions group.
The Value You Deliver
•	Deliver high quality, innovative and maintainable software solutions in an agile environment.
•	Actively contribute to test automation and practices.
•	Demonstrate strong leadership, communication, and presentation skills.
•	Experience working with distributed teams.
•	Understanding of fundamental data design principles and application design.
•	Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills.
•	Ability to quickly learn, adapt and thrive to meet the needs of a fast paced, changing environment.
•	Performing application maintenance and ensure information security controls
•	Provide timely status updates, issue resolutions, and step-by-step instructions on usability questions
•	Collaborate with Product, Execution, and other support teams to resolve or escalate user inquiries
•	Based on support queue trends, make recommendations for innovation and automation to reduce volume.

Dynamic Working
Fidelity’s hybrid working model blends the best of both onsite and offsite work experiences. Working onsite is important for our business strategy and our culture. We also value the benefits that working offsite offers associates. Most hybrid roles require associates to work onsite every other week (all business days) in a Fidelity office.
